{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778938732,"nonce":"9aAmtqZXSo8QJfnFbcLM6/+SzZ4=","message":"## Proposed implementation spec: canonical Mandible work ledger\n\n### Design stance\nMandible should become canonical for issue/work/comment/relationship state. `git-bug` should become an import/export adapter, not a hot-path dependency. That is the only design that really solves the recurring repo-lock and slow-query problems while also giving the graph enough typed data to become a stable product surface.\n\nThis should not become a generic Linear clone. The ledger should model the things Mandible actually orchestrates: issues, comments, labels, typed issue relationships, work units, sessions, conversations, auth requests, branches, commits/resolutions, handoffs, and provider/artifact provenance. Markdown remains the human-readable body/comment format, but not the data model.\n\n### Canonical identity model\nUse stable Mandible-owned IDs internally, plus aliases for external/public references.\n\nRecommended shape:\n\n- `ledger_issues.id`: canonical internal ID, stable and globally unique.\n- `ledger_issue_aliases`: maps canonical IDs to external/display IDs such as `git-bug:\u003crepo_id\u003e:097d2b7`, short issue IDs, and future GitHub issue IDs.\n- Routes and CLI should accept any unambiguous alias or prefix, but every stored relationship should use canonical IDs.\n- Existing short git-bug IDs remain user-facing where unambiguous. If a collision appears across repos, UI should disambiguate as `\u003crepo\u003e/\u003cshort-id\u003e`.\n\nThis avoids painting Mandible into a corner where global work state depends on git-bug's repo-local ID space.\n\n### Core schema\nAdd sequential `src/db.ts` migrations for a first-class ledger. Names are illustrative, but the structure should be close to this:\n\n```sql\nledger_issues (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  repo_id TEXT,\n  title TEXT NOT NULL,\n  body TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',\n  status TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(status IN ('open','closed')),\n  resolution TEXT,\n  priority TEXT,\n  kind TEXT,\n  author_actor_id TEXT,\n  author_display TEXT,\n  source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'mandible',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  closed_at INTEGER,\n  synced_at INTEGER,\n  sync_state TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'dirty'\n);\n\nledger_issue_aliases (\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  alias TEXT NOT NULL,\n  alias_kind TEXT NOT NULL,\n  repo_id TEXT,\n  external_id TEXT,\n  source TEXT NOT NULL,\n  is_primary INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (alias_kind, repo_id, alias)\n);\n\nledger_comments (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  body TEXT NOT NULL,\n  author_actor_id TEXT,\n  author_actor_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  author_display TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'mandible',\n  external_id TEXT,\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER,\n  deleted_at INTEGER\n);\n\nledger_labels (\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  label TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'mandible',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (issue_id, label)\n);\n\nledger_relationships (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  source_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  target_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  target_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  relationship_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  relationship_class TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'semantic',\n  source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'mandible',\n  confidence TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'observed',\n  metadata_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  UNIQUE(source_type, source_id, target_type, target_id, relationship_type)\n);\n\nledger_events (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  entity_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  entity_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  event_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  actor_id TEXT,\n  actor_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source TEXT NOT NULL,\n  external_id TEXT,\n  payload_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  occurred_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  observed_at INTEGER NOT NULL\n);\n\nledger_sync_jobs (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  adapter TEXT NOT NULL,\n  repo_id TEXT,\n  direction TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(direction IN ('import','export','bidirectional')),\n  status TEXT NOT NULL,\n  started_at INTEGER,\n  finished_at INTEGER,\n  cursor_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  counts_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  error TEXT\n);\n```\n\nIndexes should cover common UI paths: issue repo/status/updated, aliases, comments by issue/date, relationships by source and target, events by entity/date, sync jobs by adapter/status/repo.\n\n### Service boundary\nCreate a ledger service module, probably `src/ledger/`, rather than letting routes write SQL directly.\n\nMinimum modules:\n\n- `ledger-store.ts`: transactional SQLite reads/writes and alias resolution.\n- `ledger-types.ts`: backend types shared by routes and adapters.\n- `ledger-events.ts`: append-only event helpers and SSE broadcast helpers.\n- `git-bug-adapter.ts`: import/export only.\n- `ledger-graph-adapter.ts`: graph projection from ledger rows.\n\nEvery user-visible mutation should go through a ledger command method that writes the current-state table and the event log in one transaction, then broadcasts an SSE event. Examples: `createIssue`, `updateIssue`, `addComment`, `setStatus`, `setLabels`, `upsertRelationship`, `linkSession`, `linkAuthRequest`, `recordResolution`.\n\n### Git-bug import/export\nImport/export must be first-class and testable, but isolated from normal reads/writes.\n\nImport:\n\n- Enumerate registered repos from `work_repos`.\n- Read git-bug issue JSON and map issue body, comments, status, labels, author, timestamps, and parent labels into ledger rows.\n- Preserve git-bug IDs in `ledger_issue_aliases` and comment external IDs.\n- Convert `parent:\u003cid\u003e` labels into `ledger_relationships` of type `parent_child` while retaining the raw label for compatibility.\n- Extract obvious cross-references into typed `related` or `references` relationships only if deterministic enough; otherwise store as derived candidates, not authoritative semantic edges.\n- Run idempotently: repeated imports must not duplicate issues/comments/relationships.\n\nExport:\n\n- Export ledger-created/updated issues, comments, status, and labels back to git-bug for compatibility.\n- Export only dirty records for a repo, and mark sync state on success.\n- Store the external IDs generated by git-bug so comments are never duplicated.\n- Run as explicit sync jobs, not inside normal issue/comment/status endpoints.\n\nConflict policy, recommended first version:\n\n- Mandible wins for canonical status/title/body/labels when records are dirty locally.\n- External-only comments import as comments because comments are append-only enough.\n- External divergence in title/body/status/labels becomes a sync conflict event and visible warning, not a silent overwrite.\n- A stuck git-bug lock marks the sync job failed/retryable and does not block the UI.\n\n### Existing API integration\nPreserve current issue endpoints where possible, but change their backing implementation:\n\n- `GET /api/issues`: read from `ledger_issues`, grouped by `work_repos` repo identity.\n- `GET /api/issues/find/:issueId`: resolve aliases/prefixes through ledger.\n- `GET /api/issues/:repoId/:issueId`: resolve repo plus alias to canonical issue ID, then return ledger issue detail.\n- `POST /api/issues/:repoId/:issueId/comment`: write `ledger_comments`, not git-bug.\n- `POST /api/issues/:repoId/:issueId/status`: update ledger status/resolution, not git-bug.\n- `POST /api/issues/:repoId/:issueId/label`: update `ledger_labels`, not git-bug.\n- Add canonical endpoints such as `/api/ledger/issues/:id` or `/api/issues/by-id/:id` only if they simplify frontend code.\n\n`IssueScanner` should stop being the normal read/write path. It can be retained as a git-bug import helper or compatibility adapter during transition.\n\n### Work-unit, auth, session, and commit integration\nExisting SQLite tables should be integrated rather than duplicated.\n\nWork units:\n\n- Add `ledger_issue_id` to `work_units` and backfill from aliases.\n- Keep `issue_id` and `repo_id` temporarily for compatibility, but future code should use `ledger_issue_id` for joins.\n- Work unit lifecycle transitions should append ledger events and graph relationships.\n\nSessions:\n\n- Add `ledger_issue_id` to `session_issues`, or introduce `ledger_session_issue_links` if compatibility is cleaner.\n- Historical sessions should appear in issue detail, not as default issue-graph boxes.\n- Active/idle sessions should be available as live actors through a graph overlay/query.\n\nAuth requests:\n\n- Normalize `auth_requests.issue_ids` / `auth_requests.issues` into a link table such as `ledger_auth_issue_links(auth_request_id, ledger_issue_id, relationship_type, created_at)`.\n- On successful merge/auth completion, update ledger status/resolution first, add resolution/auth events, and let git-bug export follow asynchronously.\n- In issue graph mode, auth requests should normally be rendered as issue-attached resolution/action evidence rather than standalone nodes. In auth/work modes, they remain standalone graph nodes.\n\nCommits/resolutions:\n\n- Backfill `issue_resolutions` into ledger relationships/events.\n- Commit trailers should resolve through aliases and store canonical ledger issue IDs.\n- Commit messages can still carry short aliases for human readability.\n\nActors:\n\n- Add a simple actor convention now: `mandible_user`, `agent`, `system`, `external_adapter`.\n- Comments from Mandible UI use configurable Mandible user display identity.\n- Agent-authored comments include the session/agent identity when known.\n- Imported git-bug comments preserve external author display and source.\n\n### Graph integration\nThe graph should become a projection of the ledger plus existing operational tables.\n\nChanges:\n\n- Issue mode reads `ledger_issues` and `ledger_relationships` for issue nodes/edges.\n- Parent/child, blocks, duplicate, related, fixed-by, caused-by, implements, tests, and references are typed relationships, not label/body parsing at render time.\n- Auth requests become issue node annotations/shelves by default in issue mode.\n- Work mode includes work units, branches, sessions, auth requests, commits, and provider artifacts as first-class nodes.\n- Activity mode becomes recent ledger events plus live sessions/auth queue state.\n- Edge labels should be off by default; edge type belongs in hover/detail/toggle.\n- Umbrella/child layout should be deterministic: parent issue plus regularly spaced child issue subgraph, not force layout.\n- Session parent/child structures should also be deterministic or collapsed by default.\n- Dead sessions should not clutter the main graph; they belong in issue detail history.\n- Active/idle sessions should be represented as small live actor glyphs attached to current issue/work/action context, not as full issue-like rectangles.\n\nThe graph API should return enough display metadata to support this without provider-specific hardcoding: node annotations, collapsed child counts, relation groups, action descriptors, warnings, and sync/conflict state.\n\n### UI integration\nIssues UI and graph detail should share issue detail components.\n\nIssue detail should show:\n\n- Title, status, resolution, priority, labels, repo, aliases.\n- Markdown body.\n- Comments with actor/source badges.\n- Timeline/event log.\n- Typed relationships, editable later.\n- Work unit state and branch/worktree state.\n- Linked sessions: active/idle first, historical collapsed.\n- Linked auth requests/resolution shelf.\n- Sync state and export/import warnings.\n- Add-comment box writing directly to the ledger.\n\nGraph detail pane should reuse the same issue detail component in a compact mode. Double-click or explicit action can still navigate to the full Issues tab.\n\n### Real-time and operational behavior\nNormal ledger writes should be fast local SQLite transactions followed by SSE events. The UI should update without rescanning git-bug.\n\nRecommended SSE events:\n\n- `ledger:issue:created`\n- `ledger:issue:updated`\n- `ledger:comment:created`\n- `ledger:relationship:upserted`\n- `ledger:sync:updated`\n- `ledger:event:created`\n\nGit-bug sync jobs should be queued/serialized per repo with status visible in the UI. They should have retries, timeouts, and explicit error messages. Do not delete git-bug lock files automatically in the normal path.\n\n### Migration and rollout\nImplementation should be staged but aim for a complete stable model now.\n\n1. Add schema, types, and `LedgerStore` service with transactional command methods and unit tests.\n2. Implement git-bug import into ledger with idempotency tests using fixture JSON and, if practical, a temp repo smoke test.\n3. Backfill existing Mandible DB links: work units, session issue links, auth request issue links, and issue resolutions.\n4. Switch issue routes and `mandible issue` CLI to ledger-backed reads/writes.\n5. Add export/sync jobs and visible sync status.\n6. Switch graph issue/activity/work projections to ledger IDs and typed relationships.\n7. Update Issues UI and graph detail pane to render ledger body/comments/timeline/relationships/auth shelf/session history.\n8. Keep compatibility fields/routes until downstream callers are migrated; remove or deprecate only after verification.\n\n### Verification plan\nMinimum verification before merge:\n\n- Migration tests on fresh and upgraded DBs.\n- Ledger command unit tests for create/update/comment/status/label/relationship/event transactions.\n- Alias resolver tests, including ambiguous short IDs.\n- Git-bug import idempotency tests preserving body/comments/status/labels/parent labels/auth-resolved comments.\n- Git-bug export tests against fixture/fake adapter; temp repo smoke test if stable enough.\n- Route tests for existing issue APIs backed by ledger.\n- Work-unit/session/auth integration tests resolving canonical ledger IDs.\n- Graph tests proving issue relationships come from ledger and auth requests are attached/omitted according to mode.\n- UI build plus browser smoke: issue list/detail, add comment, graph issue mode, graph work mode, sync warning surface.\n- Full `npm test` and `npm run build`.\n\n### Non-goals for the first implementation\n\n- Full GitHub Issues adapter.\n- Supporting every external tracker.\n- Replacing all Mandible tabs with graph views.\n- Full semantic relationship auto-classification from arbitrary issue prose.\n- Public multi-user SaaS permissions.\n- Removing git-bug compatibility immediately.\n\n### Decisions I recommend unless MLL disagrees\n\n- Mandible canonical state wins over git-bug after import.\n- Git-bug sync is explicit/retryable and never blocks normal issue reads/writes.\n- Internal IDs are canonical; short git-bug IDs are aliases.\n- Auth requests are issue-attached evidence in issue mode but first-class nodes in auth/work modes.\n- Dead sessions are historical issue detail, not default graph nodes.\n- Active/idle sessions are live actor glyphs/overlays, not full graph cards.\n- Graph is a projection of the ledger; the graph itself is not the canonical store.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}